          "source": "theory Presentation_Transport\n  imports Presentation_Closure\nbegin\n\nsection \\<open>Presentations of one independently fixed subject correspond\\<close>\n\ndefinition presentation_transport ::\n  \"('a \\<Rightarrow> 'p \\<Rightarrow> bool) \\<Rightarrow> ('a \\<Rightarrow> 'q \\<Rightarrow> bool) \\<Rightarrow>\n    'p \\<Rightarrow> 'q \\<Rightarrow> bool\" where\n  \"presentation_transport R S p q \\<longleftrightarrow> (\\<exists>a. R a p \\<and> S a q)\"\n\nlemma presentation_transport_relation:\n  \"presentation_transport R S = presented_relation R S (=)\"\n  by (intro ext) (auto simp: presentation_transport_def presented_relation_def)\n\nlemma presentation_transport_reverse:\n  \"presentation_transport R S p q \\<longleftrightarrow> presentation_transport S R q p\"\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def)\n\nlocale presentation_change =\n  source: presentation_class R D A + target: presentation_class S D B\n  for R :: \"'a \\<Rightarrow> 'p \\<Rightarrow> bool\" and D A\n    and S :: \"'a \\<Rightarrow> 'q \\<Rightarrow> bool\" and B\nbegin\n\nlemma at:\n  assumes \"R a p\" \"S b q\"\n  shows \"presentation_transport R S p q \\<longleftrightarrow> a=b\"\n  using assms source.recovery target.recovery\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; blast)\n\nlemma forward:\n  assumes \"R a p\"\n  shows \"presentation_transport R S p q \\<longleftrightarrow> S a q\"\n  using assms source.recovery by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; blast)\n\nlemma backward:\n  assumes \"S a q\"\n  shows \"presentation_transport R S p q \\<longleftrightarrow> R a p\"\n  using assms target.recovery by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; blast)\n\ntheorem source_total:\n  assumes \"A p\"\n  shows \"\\<exists>q. presentation_transport R S p q\"\n  using source.admitted[OF assms] source.subject_boundary target.total\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; blast)\n\ntheorem target_total:\n  assumes \"B q\"\n  shows \"\\<exists>p. presentation_transport R S p q\"\n  using target.admitted[OF assms] target.subject_boundary source.total\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; blast)\n\nlemma boundaries:\n  assumes \"presentation_transport R S p q\"\n  shows \"A p \\<and> B q\"\n  using assms source.presentation_boundary target.presentation_boundary\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def)\n\ntheorem predicate_transport:\n  assumes \"presentation_transport R S p q\"\n  shows \"presented_predicate R P p \\<longleftrightarrow> presented_predicate S P q\"\n  using assms source.recovery target.recovery\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def presented_predicate_def; blast)\n\ntheorem set_transport:\n  \"presented_set (presentation_transport R S) (presented_set R X) = presented_set S X\"\n  using source.recovery source.total target.subject_boundary\n  by (auto simp: presented_set_def presentation_transport_def; blast)\n\nend\n\ntheorem presentation_transport_identity:\n  assumes \"presentation_class R D A\"\n  shows \"presentation_transport R R p p \\<longleftrightarrow> A p\"\n  using presentation_class.admissible_iff[OF assms]\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def)\n\ntheorem presentation_transport_compose:\n  assumes first: \"presentation_class R D A\" and middle: \"presentation_class S D B\"\n  shows \"(\\<exists>q. presentation_transport R S p q \\<and> presentation_transport S T q r)\n    \\<longleftrightarrow> presentation_transport R T p r\"\nproof -\n  interpret first: presentation_class R D A by (rule first)\n  interpret middle: presentation_class S D B by (rule middle)\n  show ?thesis using first.subject_boundary middle.recovery middle.total\n    by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; blast)\nqed\n\nsection \\<open>Every relation transports through the same correspondence\\<close>\n\ntheorem presented_relation_transport:\n  assumes left: \"presentation_class A D X\" and left': \"presentation_class A' D X'\"\n    and right: \"presentation_class B E Y\" and right': \"presentation_class B' E Y'\"\n    and inputs: \"presentation_transport A A' p p'\" \"presentation_transport B B' q q'\"\n  shows \"presented_relation A B L p q \\<longleftrightarrow> presented_relation A' B' L p' q'\"\nproof -\n  interpret left: presentation_class A D X by (rule left)\n  interpret left': presentation_class A' D X' by (rule left')\n  interpret right: presentation_class B E Y by (rule right)\n  interpret right': presentation_class B' E Y' by (rule right')\n  show ?thesis using inputs left.recovery left'.recovery right.recovery right'.recovery\n    by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def presented_relation_def; blast)\nqed\n\ntheorem presented_relation_compose_across:\n  assumes middle: \"presentation_class B D X\" and other: \"presentation_class B' D X'\"\n  shows \"(\\<exists>q u. presented_relation A B L p q \\<and> presentation_transport B B' q u \\<and>\n      presented_relation B' C M u r) \\<longleftrightarrow>\n    presented_relation A C (\\<lambda>a c. \\<exists>b. D b \\<and> L a b \\<and> M b c) p r\"\nproof -\n  interpret middle: presentation_class B D X by (rule middle)\n  interpret other: presentation_class B' D X' by (rule other)\n  show ?thesis\n  proof\n    assume \"\\<exists>q u. presented_relation A B L p q \\<and> presentation_transport B B' q u \\<and>\n      presented_relation B' C M u r\"\n    then obtain q u a b k h c where first: \"A a p\" \"B b q\" \"L a b\"\n      and bridge: \"B k q\" \"B' k u\" and last: \"B' h u\" \"C c r\" \"M h c\"\n      unfolding presentation_transport_def presented_relation_def by blast\n    have same: \"b=k\" \"k=h\"\n      using middle.recovery[OF first(2) bridge(1)] other.recovery[OF bridge(2) last(1)] by auto\n    have domain: \"D b\" by (rule middle.subject_boundary[OF first(2)])\n    show \"presented_relation A C (\\<lambda>a c. \\<exists>b. D b \\<and> L a b \\<and> M b c) p r\"\n      using first last domain same unfolding presented_relation_def by blast\n  next\n    assume \"presented_relation A C (\\<lambda>a c. \\<exists>b. D b \\<and> L a b \\<and> M b c) p r\"\n    then obtain a c b where parts: \"A a p\" \"C c r\" \"D b\" \"L a b\" \"M b c\"\n      unfolding presented_relation_def by blast\n    obtain q where first: \"B b q\" using middle.total[OF parts(3)] by blast\n    obtain u where second: \"B' b u\" using other.total[OF parts(3)] by blast\n    show \"\\<exists>q u. presented_relation A B L p q \\<and> presentation_transport B B' q u \\<and>\n      presented_relation B' C M u r\"\n      by (rule exI[of _ q], rule exI[of _ u])\n        (use parts first second in \\<open>auto simp: presentation_transport_def presented_relation_def\\<close>)\n  qed\nqed\n\nsection \\<open>Specialization retains every presentation of the selected subjects\\<close>\n\ntheorem presentation_transport_subdomain:\n  assumes source: \"presentation_class R D A\"\n  shows \"presentation_transport (\\<lambda>a p. E a \\<and> R a p) (\\<lambda>a q. E a \\<and> S a q) p q\n    \\<longleftrightarrow> presentation_transport R S p q \\<and> presented_predicate R E p\"\nproof -\n  interpret source: presentation_class R D A by (rule source)\n  show ?thesis using source.recovery\n    by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def presented_predicate_def; blast)\nqed\n\nsection \\<open>Component correspondences compose without choosing representatives\\<close>\n\nlemma presentation_transport_product:\n  \"presentation_transport (\\<lambda>z p. R (fst z) (fst p) \\<and> S (snd z) (snd p))\n      (\\<lambda>z p. R' (fst z) (fst p) \\<and> S' (snd z) (snd p)) (p,q) (p',q')\n    \\<longleftrightarrow> presentation_transport R R' p p' \\<and> presentation_transport S S' q q'\"\n  by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def; metis fst_conv snd_conv)\n\nlemma presentation_transport_lists:\n  \"presentation_transport (list_all2 R) (list_all2 S) ps qs \\<longleftrightarrow>\n    list_all2 (presentation_transport R S) ps qs\"\nproof (induction ps arbitrary: qs)\n  case Nil\n  then show ?case by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def list_all2_Nil2)\nnext\n  case (Cons p ps)\n  have tail: \"presentation_transport (list_all2 R) (list_all2 S) ps us \\<longleftrightarrow>\n      list_all2 (presentation_transport R S) ps us\" for us by (rule Cons.IH)\n  have step: \"presentation_transport (list_all2 R) (list_all2 S) (p#ps) (q#us) \\<longleftrightarrow>\n      presentation_transport R S p q \\<and> presentation_transport (list_all2 R) (list_all2 S) ps us\" for q us\n    by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def list_all2_Cons2; blast)\n  show ?case\n  proof (cases qs)\n    case Nil\n    then show ?thesis by (auto simp: presentation_transport_def list_all2_Nil2)\n  next\n    case (Cons q us)\n    then show ?thesis by (simp only: step tail list_all2_Cons)\n  qed\nqed\n\nsection \\<open>Local recursive contracts give transport of the completed meanings\\<close>\n\ntheorem presentation_transport_least_fixed_points:\n  fixes F :: \"'a set \\<Rightarrow> 'a set\"\n    and G :: \"'p set \\<Rightarrow> 'p set\" and H :: \"'q set \\<Rightarrow> 'q set\"\n  assumes source: \"presentation_class R D A\" and target: \"presentation_class S D B\"\n    and semantic_mono: \"mono F\" and source_mono: \"mono G\" and target_mono: \"mono H\"\n    and boundary: \"\\<And>X. X\\<subseteq>{a. D a} \\<Longrightarrow> F X\\<subseteq>{a. D a}\"\n    and source_step: \"\\<And>X. X\\<subseteq>{a. D a} \\<Longrightarrow>\n      G (presented_set R X)=presented_set R (F X)\"\n    and target_step: \"\\<And>X. X\\<subseteq>{a. D a} \\<Longrightarrow>\n      H (presented_set S X)=presented_set S (F X)\"\n  shows \"presented_set (presentation_transport R S) (lfp G)=lfp H\"\nproof -\n  interpret change: presentation_change R D A S B by (rule presentation_change.intro[OF source target])\n  have first: \"lfp G=presented_set R (lfp F)\"\n    by (rule presented_least_fixed_point_on[OF semantic_mono source_mono boundary source_step])\n  have second: \"lfp H=presented_set S (lfp F)\"\n    by (rule presented_least_fixed_point_on[OF semantic_mono target_mono boundary target_step])\n  show ?thesis by (simp only: first second change.set_transport)\nqed\n\ntext \\<open>\n  The subject type and domain are fixed independently of a use. Two exact\n  classes over that same domain supply a total correspondence in both\n  directions. A correspondence contains every pair recovering the same\n  subject. Its identity, reversal, composition, and relation laws therefore\n  require no selected representative, matching raw syntax, or pair-specific\n  semantic proof. Specialization restricts subjects and retains all their\n  presentations; the existing subdomain class theorem supplies its coverage.\n\n  This correspondence differs from composed_presentation: that construction\n  recovers a complete intermediate presentation, as required by quotation.\n  Correspondence instead allows intermediate material to vary while its\n  independently fixed subject stays the same. The explicit reading relations\n  remain part of the contract. Erasing their context does not give a sound\n  union of overlapping raw grammars.\n\n  The laws are mathematical transport contracts. Each actual reader establishes\n  its own exact relation or consequence equation at the owning notion's\n  boundary. These laws then transport its meaning uniformly. They do not\n  compile arbitrary relations, execute a choice of representative, or change\n  the actual body stored in a quoted source.\n\\<close>\n\nend\n",
