          "theory": "Factor_Collection_Comparisons",
          "source": "theory Factor_Collection_Comparisons\n  imports Factor_Key_Fibres Factor_Finite_Set_Presentations\nbegin\n\nsection \\<open>One complete encoded collection determines every compared output\\<close>\n\ntheorem encoded_collection_comparison:\n  assumes injective: \"inj f\"\n    and source: \"data_collection_presents (\\<lambda>a t. D a \\<and> t=f a) A p\"\n    and data: \"\\<And>a. a\\<in>A \\<Longrightarrow> term_formed (f a) \\<and> self_contained_term (f a)\"\n  shows \"(6,Pair_Term p q)\\<in>positive_meaning bag_comparison_system \\<longleftrightarrow>\n    data_collection_presents (\\<lambda>a t. D a \\<and> t=f a) A q\"\nproof -\n  have reading: \"data_collection_presents (\\<lambda>a t. D a \\<and> t=f a) A t \\<longleftrightarrow>\n      (\\<exists>xs. distinct xs \\<and> set xs=A \\<and> (\\<forall>a\\<in>set xs. D a) \\<and>\n        t=data_list_term (map f xs))\" for t\n    by (auto simp: data_collection_presents_constrain data_collection_presents_function)\n  obtain xs where first: \"distinct xs\" \"set xs=A\" \"\\<forall>a\\<in>set xs. D a\"\n    \"p=data_list_term (map f xs)\" using source by (simp only: reading; blast)\n  have fields: \"data_elements (map f xs)\" using data first(2) by auto\n  have compared: \"(6,Pair_Term p q)\\<in>positive_meaning bag_comparison_system \\<longleftrightarrow>\n      (\\<exists>ys. q=data_list_term (map f ys) \\<and> mset xs=mset ys)\"\n    by (simp only: first(4) bag_comparison_encoded[OF injective fields])\n  show ?thesis\n  proof (simp only: compared reading, rule iffI)\n    assume \"\\<exists>ys. q=data_list_term (map f ys) \\<and> mset xs=mset ys\"\n    then obtain ys where second: \"q=data_list_term (map f ys)\" \"mset xs=mset ys\" by blast\n    have same: \"set xs=set ys\" \"distinct xs=distinct ys\"\n      using mset_eq_setD[OF second(2)] mset_eq_imp_distinct_iff[OF second(2)] by blast+\n    show \"\\<exists>ys. distinct ys \\<and> set ys=A \\<and> (\\<forall>a\\<in>set ys. D a) \\<and>\n        q=data_list_term (map f ys)\"\n      by (rule exI[of _ ys]) (use first second same in blast)\n  next\n    assume \"\\<exists>ys. distinct ys \\<and> set ys=A \\<and> (\\<forall>a\\<in>set ys. D a) \\<and>\n        q=data_list_term (map f ys)\"\n    then obtain ys where second: \"distinct ys\" \"set ys=A\" \"q=data_list_term (map f ys)\" by blast\n    have same: \"mset xs=mset ys\"\n      using set_eq_iff_mset_eq_distinct[OF first(1) second(1)] first(2) second(2) by blast\n    show \"\\<exists>ys. q=data_list_term (map f ys) \\<and> mset xs=mset ys\"\n      using second(3) same by blast\n  qed\nqed\n\ntext \\<open>\n  The existing bag comparison accounts for every output term. For an injective\n  element encoding and a complete distinct source enumeration, equality of\n  bags gives exactly every enumeration of the same finite collection. The\n  element domain and data formation remain explicit. This derived law does\n  not identify equal-looking presentations of different element notions.\n\\<close>\n\nend\n",
